you talk about one of the final  engagements  that um harry and megan had one of their  final formal engagements and um  it was a moment in the state room and  you said megan began to cry  and that she said she can't believe this  is it and you also talked about a moment  in march of this year where she hugged  you  and she said to you it didn't have to be  this way  what did you take from that statement  because there could be so much meaning  in those words it didn't have to be this  way i think that final engagement at  buckingham palace not only was a  poignant moment this was a  member of the royal family taking their  sort of last steps as a working royal  uh in a palace setting for me as a royal  correspondent was surreal  but i think to see megan so emotional in  that moment and so vulnerable  just showed how far she felt that she  had been pushed  at that point the couple had really done  everything they could to make it work  as we know at the start of the year they  presented that road map to  what we've referred to as a half in half  out working model and  the fact that that was rejected and they  were forced into this position of  stepping away  that is what didn't have to be this way  and i think that's what the couple  really found difficult to come to terms  with as they headed off back to canada  that their family hadn't seen the  grievances that they brought to the  table  or try to be flexible in any way  whatsoever  as is often the case in the royal family  duty comes first  and in that instance that what they  proposed just wasn't going to work  for the institution of the monarchy the  decision that  i have made for my wife and i to step  back  is not one i made lightly do you feel  like if harry  wouldn't have married megan that he  would still be a part of  the firm and never would have left i  think whoever harry married would have  been  that gateway to exploring a different  kind of life to  challenge the work settings around him  harry someone that i think has always  needed a teammate to really complete the  picture  um i think sometimes being on royal  engagements with him when he was working  by himself  i always felt that he would really  benefit from someone by himself he would  say  so much more and i think in some ways  we've seen him emboldened  uh by his relationship with megan she's  given him confidence or at least that  relationship  and being a father has given him  confidence to speak out and be more  vocal about things  in a way that he hadn't before i would  argue that if harry had said to megan  let's stick it out for another five  years  that she would have really gone for that  because as we heard from the sources  speaking in the book she gave up  everything she was willing to give her  life to it and  the way it ended so quickly i do not  think was what she had in mind  yeah well i guess and also thank you for  asking because not many people have  asked if i'm okay  but it's  it's a very real thing to be going  through behind the scenes  do you think she her mind just didn't  really grasp it or is she too much of an  individual  to ever just be able to do it i think  there's a difference between being  warned before marrying someone like  prince harry that your life will change  for good that the press  will not leave you alone and to be  reminded of what diana went through  but particularly during those very  difficult times after her divorce with  prince charles  and these are things that megan would  have gone into that marriage knowing  but it's very different to know it than  to live it and i think whilst we saw  megan  put on a very brave front publicly as  the book tells behind the scenes she  really struggled with some of those  intrusions and just to have so many  people involved in her life  we're a fantastic team we know we are do  you feel like that harry and megan have  any responsibility in this  at all it can't just be the everything  that they did is right and everything  that everybody else did  is wrong i think really where it fell  apart is the fact that harry and megan  did want to do things differently that  they did want to  restructure the way that they worked  within the institution but  you have to remember this is a firm that  has been around for a very long time and  things work very well the way they do  you can't just  go in and try and change things and  expect everyone to agree with you  and i think that there are times like  that where we saw harry and megan arrive  in the uk at the start of the year with  this road map of how they wanted to work  moving forward i know that for other  members of the family  they felt their noses slightly put out  of joints at that time because  as one aide said to me it was like they  just arrived and handed in a rider  and said that charles was going to pick  up the bill and they were going to fly  back to  canada and get on with their new chapter  and of course it doesn't work like that  there are many layers to go through it  is an institution  there is tradition within that that has  to be respected and so  i think in some ways their eagerness to  bring change and do things differently  also got them into trouble because  that just was never going to work within  the space that they wanted to do it  you
 

